Limit: ConversationTurnCoordinator.dispatch commits its dispatch row in a transaction of its own, so a lane that claimed in one transaction and dispatched in the next left a claimed, undispatched turn and a spent nonce when the dispatch write failed or the process stopped between the two commits (R1062-01)
Limit: the coordinator claims without turn_claim_json, so IngressGuard.prune's claimed-row exemption could not see an external-lane turn, and the expired ingress row's payload is the only address a COMPLETED receipt's owner reply can be given (R1062-02)
Ruled-out: a public dispatch step that only writes the row, with the caller sending after its own commit | it is markDispatching public beside dispatch again, rejected because a caller that can pick the order will eventually pick the wrong one; dispatchOnCommit takes the send and Db.afterCommit holds it until the outermost commit
Ruled-out: a prune exemption scoped to the external lane's guard | ownerReplyAddressFor reads the source payload whichever lane admitted the message, so the exemption is keyed on the canonical ledger for every channel rather than on the external lane alone
Warn: dispatchOnCommit does not await send; what send throws surfaces from the commit that ran it, after the dispatch row is durable, so a send must report its own delivery failure
